# HDR, Panoramas, Focus Stacking, and Compositing

Advanced multi-image techniques for extending what a single capture can achieve.

## HDR (High Dynamic Range)

Combine multiple bracketed exposures (-2, 0, +2 EV) for extended dynamic range. Best for high contrast scenes like landscapes with bright sky and dark foreground. Merge in HDR software, then tone map for a natural look.

## Panoramas

Stitch multiple overlapping photos (30-50% overlap) for wide views. Keep camera level with a tripod. Merge in Lightroom, Photoshop, or PTGui.

## Focus Stacking

Combine multiple photos at different focus distances for extended depth of field. Best for macro photography and landscapes.

## Compositing

Combine elements from multiple photos. Requires Photoshop. Examples: replace sky, add moon, combine people.

Related to [[Post-Processing]].
